  "Id": 294,
  "Title": "AKU-IED, Pakistan Wins UNICEF Grant Award for Research",
  "NewsSubTitle": null,
  "NewsSummary": "AKU-IED, Pakistan has won a UNICEF grant award of US$ 300,000/- for a project titled \u201cGenerate knowledge and evidence on the contribution of education for social cohesion and resilience and to support and inform programming for UNICEF and partners\u201d.",
  "GlobalNews": false,
  "AlternateNewsTitle": null,
  "AlternateNewsSubtitle": null,
  "AlternateNewsSummary": null,
  "NewsContent": "<div class=\"ExternalClass698783BCB8474EB3B8CCCB4CCC1BE8BF\"><div>\u200bAKU-IED, Pakistan has won a UNICEF grant award of US$ 300,000/- for a project titled \u201cGenerate knowledge and evidence on the contribution of education for social cohesion and resilience and to support and inform programming for UNICEF and partners\u201d.\u200b</div><div><br></div><div>The project will include the following activities&#58;\u200b\u200b\u200b</div><div><ul><li>Technical oversight for research for UNICEF\u2019s implementing partners<br></li><li>Producing comprehensive qualitative and quantitative research<br></li><li>Hosting conferences for dissemination and support of research on education, youth, social cohesion and resilience<br></li></ul></div><div>The one-year project activities will facilitate AKU-IED's efforts to expand and enhance its research and scholarship capacity and further strengthen AKU-IED\u2019s mission to deliver effective education and interventions in the education sector. It will also assist in developing its young faculty\u2019s capacity in research, project management and conference organisation.</div><div><br></div><div>The AKU-IED faculty project team includes Dr Alan DeYoung, Dr Dilshad Ashraf, Dr Parveen Roy and Ms Cassandra Fernandes.\u200b</div></div>",
